WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.309 align:start position:0%
 
after  days of loyalist fury on the streets of  northern ireland  these were used in a nationalist area  confronting police  fireworks were launched at the police  line on springfield road in belfast  youth smashed lumps of concrete to hurl  at officers  for the first time in six years water  cannon was deployed  in northern ireland police water cannon  used against protesters on the streets  of belfast this was a site  many here thought have been consigned to  history  but as we move towards the 23rd  anniversary of the signing  of the good friday agreement this  weekend this goes to show just how far  and how much work has to be done towards  reconciliation here  in northern ireland  last night's trouble came after a week  of protests from loyalists  angry over the northern ireland protocol  which they say brought in an irish sea  border  and the failure to prosecute sinn fein  members for breaching coronavirus  regulations  on wednesday night came clashes between  the two communities  in what police described as the worst  violence in years  the scenes that we saw were absolutely  disgraceful  in terms of the serious criminal acts  that were being carried out  and the violent disorder that was taking  place and it needs to be condemned in  the strongest possible terms  boris johnson has appeal for cam along  with his irish counterpart mijo martin  and now the white house we are concerned  by the violence in northern ireland  and we join the british irish and  northern irish leaders in their calls  for calm  we remain steadfast supporters of a  secure and prosperous northern ireland  in which all communities have a voice  and enjoy the gains of the hard-won  peace  but no one knows for sure who's  orchestrating the ongoing trouble  or if they're listening to the  politicians  there will be more talks today but many  here are apprehensive at what the  weekend will bring  after a week of bitter confrontation  that's injured dozens  but shocked and disillusioned many many  more  stephen murphy sky news in belfast

